+### Transactional diagram automation
+
+The desktop helper exposes `diagramCommand()` and `diagramCancel()` in
+`excalidraw-app/excalidrawZ/index.js`. The command engine in
+`excalidraw-app/excalidrawZ/diagramCommands.js` validates isolated scenes before
+one undoable commit, enforces document/revision checks and per-client request
+idempotency, retains extension data, and supports inspection, graph layout,
+quality analysis and bounded snapshot rendering. The executable command manifest
+is `excalidraw-app/excalidrawZ/diagramCommandSchema.json` (line 1), returned by
+`get_capabilities`; the document identity comes from successful file loads.
+`packages/excalidraw/components/App.tsx` provides private atomic scene/assets and
+history bridges. `creators.js` bundles the ELK worker and carries edge routes into
+created arrows. `diagramCommands.test.js` covers transactions, scene relations,
+revision races, quality checks and 100/1,000-element fixtures.
+
+`excalidraw-app/excalidrawZ/creators.js:300` reserves measured connector labels
+in ELK, preserves their routed geometry and places native bound labels on clear
+segments. Cyclic graphs use ELK wrapping for readable proportions; explicit
+layout options and pinned positions remain authoritative. Quality inspection in
+`diagramCommands.js` reports `label_overlap` even inside shared frames, while
+respecting bound node text and explicitly grouped/marked illustrations.
+
+`excalidraw-app/excalidrawZ/diagramCommands.js` also reports `frame_overlap`
+for independent partially overlapping frames; full containment, frame ancestry
+and explicit intentional-overlap metadata remain valid composition choices.
